# The shop bench's performance budget, each line fixed before its first measurement (run-log 235; explore's and
# search's lines, run-log 279). test/bench/performance-budget reads this file. It never cuts work: "check" lines judge
# counts that do not depend on the machine. A "check" line fails the run when the value is over; a "report" line is
# printed against its budget only, since wall time depends on the machine (these were set for an Apple M2 laptop, z3 on
# PATH, --jobs 4, an empty cache).
#
# Questions: the scripts the solver ran from an empty cache. 120 s of prove at --jobs 4 is 480 solver-seconds; the
# 3-service bench's questions average 0.12 s of wall time each at --jobs 4, so about 1500 questions fit.
check prove.questions 1500
# search's own questions: the search run's scripts less prove's. Of the 300 s a commit's run gets, prove takes 120 s
# and explore 90 s, which leaves search 90 s, so about 1100 questions at the rate above.
check search.questions 1100
# Every question decides at the default resource limit.
check prove.undecided 0
check search.undecided 0
# The largest script and all of prove's scripts together, in bytes. z3 read a 12 MB response script in about 0.9 s
# (run-log 224), so 16 MiB keeps one script's reading near a second, and 512 MiB keeps prove's reading near 10 s at
# --jobs 4.
check script.max_bytes 16777216
check prove.script_bytes 536870912
# search's own scripts together, in bytes: the search run's less prove's. The rule above gives reading a twelfth of a
# stage's time (10 s of prove's 120 s), so search's 90 s allows 7.5 s, which is 384 MiB at --jobs 4.
check search.script_bytes 402653184
# explore runs one service after another on one core. 3-services' explore ran 70,000 to 72,000 transitions a second
# (run-log 279), so its 90 s is about 6.3 million transitions. Its states stay in memory: 3-services' take 1.6 KB each,
# and a shop state holds several tables of records, so take 4 times that; 150,000 states then keep about 1 GB.
check explore.transitions 6300000
check explore.states 150000
# Wall time in seconds.
report check.seconds 5
report prove.cold.seconds 120
report prove.cached.seconds 10
# explore alone: the explore run, from prove's cache, less the cached prove run.
report explore.seconds 90
# prove, explore and search from an empty cache.
report search.seconds 300
